marc: Python:
```python
# 2 retries, then trim and fallback
def call(cli,prompt,primary,cheap):
  for i in range(2):
    r=cli.generate(model=primary,prompt=prompt,timeout=5)
    if r.status==200: return r.text
    if r.status==429: sleep((2**i)*0.3)
  short='\n'.join(prompt.split('\n')[-3:])
  return cli.generate(model=cheap,prompt=short).text
```

jen: Add a short note: "Always preserve system/instruction block when trimming; test with eval prompts." Also mention Retry-After parsing in JS.

marc: TS snippet:
```ts
// 2 retries, honor Retry-After, then deterministic trim
async function gen(payload){
  for(let i=0;i<2;i++){
    const res=await fetch('/v1/generate',{method:'POST',body:JSON.stringify(payload)})
    if(res.status===200) return await res.json()
    if(res.status===429){const ra=res.headers.get('Retry-After');await sleep(ra?Number(ra)*1000:Math.pow(2,i)*300)}
  }
  payload.input=trimKeepSystem(payload.input,2)
  return fetch('/v1/generate?model=small-1',{method:'POST',body:JSON.stringify(payload)}).then(r=>r.json())
}
```

